window.docContents[25].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Reductions.ReductionDsl.Core/#file-Computational___Specifications___Reductions___ReductionDsl___Core":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Reductions/ReductionDsl › Core.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 3 headline theorems depend on it 699 of 1,096 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (61)structure Siginductive Tydef Ty.denoteinductive Varinductive Envdef Env.getstructure Opsdef Ops.sumdef bitsdef Ty.Fitsabbrev ValFitsdef OpsSizeHonestinductive Exprdef Expr.evaldef Expr.costdef Expr.sizedef reductionSizeBudgetstructure Samplersdef SampSizeHoneststructure Ifacedef Iface.liftPinductive Compdef iterMdef findMLdef anyMLdef mapMLdef consumeFirstMLdef foldMLdef Comp.evaldef Comp.costdef Comp.queriesdef Comp.sizestructure GameCodecdef handlerImplstructure CostedReductiondef CostedReduction.impldef CostedReduction.evaldef CostedReduction.totalCostdef CostedReduction.totalQueriesdef CostedReduction.sizeinductive Midstructure TwoStageCostedReductiondef TwoStageCostedReduction.run1def runFueldef TwoStageCostedReduction.eval1def TwoStageCostedReduction.eval2def TwoStageCostedReduction.totalCostdef TwoStageCostedReduction.totalQueriesdef TwoStageCostedReduction.sizedef AllGameQueriesFitdef supportWhendef Iface.AnswerFitsdef Expr.costAtdef Comp.pureEval?def Comp.costAtdef CostedReduction.ValidKindCostsdef CostedReduction.totalCostByKinddef CostedReduction.CostBoundedByKinddef TwoStageCostedReduction.ValidKindCostsdef TwoStageCostedReduction.totalCostByKinddef TwoStageCostedReduction.CostBoundedByKind\n\nReductionDsl: a costed deep embedding for game reductionsTrusted in part. Every definition in this file except the variable shorthands Expr.v0 to Expr.v6 is part of the trusted base (Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md): a reduction named by a headline statement is a CostedReduction or TwoStageCostedReduction value whose efficiency claims use totalCost, totalQueries, size, and the per-query-kind cost definitions (Expr.costAt, Comp.pureEval?, Comp.costAt, ValidKindCosts, totalCostByKind, CostBoundedByKind). The auxiliary size, table-cost, and dual-fuel definitions (Ty.BaseFits, OpsBaseBounded, SampBaseBounded, Ty.listDepth, Ty.NoNestedLists, Ty.HasNoTbl, Ty.treeBlocks, Expr.costWithTbl, Comp.costWithTbl, GameCodec.FitsOn, GameCodec.BaseFitsOn, CostedReduction.totalCostBounded, TwoStageCostedReduction.run1Bounded, runFuelBounded, TwoStageCostedReduction.eval1Bounded, TwoStageCostedReduction.eval2Bounded, TwoStageCostedReduction.totalCostBounded) are proof-support definitions outside every headline's closure.ReductionDsl is the first-order language in which security reductions of the computational proof stack are written. It defines pure expressions (Expr) over inspectable data types (unit, bool, nat, opt, prod, sum, list, tbl) and opaque abstract sorts S.Base accessed solely through declared operation tables (Ops); monadic programs (Comp) with coin-only Samplers, target-game oracle queries (Iface), and statically bounded loops; interpretation into VCVio OracleComp (Expr.eval, Comp.eval); structural and input-specialized step-cost, query, and syntax-size measures (cost, costAt, queries, size); and single- and two-stage transducers (CostedReduction, TwoStageCostedReduction) over source-game codecs (GameCodec). Shared operation tables, uniform samplers, and target codecs live in AtomicOps.lean, Samplers.lean, and Computational/Specifications/Reductions/ReductionDsl/TargetCodecs.lean; see Computational/docs/REDUCTION_DSL_TUTORIAL.md.The efficiency model rests on five invariants:1. Sort opacity and table honesty. Expr eliminates .base b only via Expr.op. Each table entry O.cost o bounds the work of O.eval o up to O.cost o × (max input blocks) under block measure S.sz and satisfies OpsSizeHonest; each query tag's I.qCost covers reading its argument and answer, I.uCost covers one forwarded uniform coin draw, and each coin-only sampler's constant I.smp.sCost bounds output width (SampSizeHonest). Reductions use only shared Ops, Samplers, Iface, and GameCodec tables.2. Bounded value growth. Every value-growing constructor pays at least its output growth in blocks, bit-length, or list length, so run values stay within input size plus step cost plus a run-local oracle-answer bound (Comp.fits_eval in Computational/Proofs/ReductionDsl/Size.lean).3. Single-pass black-box execution. CostedReduction.eval executes the adversary A once via simulateQ without rewinding (TwoStageCostedReduction pauses A at most once at a challenge query and resumes its continuation in stage 2), so totalCost and totalQueries bound work outside A and target queries (Computational/Proofs/ReductionDsl/Soundness.lean).4. Syntax-size bound. Because branch cost takes max over arms, step cost alone allows a depth-d decision tree to embed a 2 ^ d-entry non-uniform lookup table. Headline boundedness predicates therefore also require size ≤ reductionSizeBudget (2 ^ 24 syntax nodes; both branch arms, numeric literal bit-lengths, Ops.opSize literal payloads, and each loop body count once).5. Input-specialized per-kind cost. Expr.costAt and Comp.costAt charge branches only for the arm selected at ρ (computed via Expr.eval), and Comp.bind specializes its continuation only after an effect-free prefix (Comp.pureEval?), falling back to static k.cost after any sample, query, or monadic loop. ValidKindCosts quantifies over all states s and queries t, bounding per-query-kind work via totalCostByKind (Computational/Proofs/ReductionDsl/KindedCost.lean).\n\n\n\nstructure SigL74–79 ↗#Signature of abstract base sorts Base with carrier den and block-size measure sz (e.g. ⌈len / w⌉ for byte strings of block width w, or 1 for fixed-width values).\n\n\n\ninductive TyL83–92 ↗#First-order value types over abstract sorts S: inspectable unit, booleans, naturals, options, products, sums, finite lists, and total ℕ-indexed tables tbl t.\n\ndef Ty.denoteL94–104 ↗#Carrier of a value type.\n\ninductive VarL106–109 ↗#Typed de Bruijn variables in context Γ.\n\ninductive EnvL111–114 ↗#Evaluation environments for typed context Γ.\n\ndef Env.getL116–118 ↗#\n\nstructure OpsL120–128 ↗#Table of primitive operations over S with semantics eval, step cost cost, and embedded literal size opSize (charged in Expr.size; 0 by default).\n\ndef Ops.sumL130–139 ↗#Disjoint union of two operation tables over S.\n\ndef bitsL141–142 ↗#Bit-length cost ⌊log₂ n⌋ + 1 of a natural-number literal or constant operand n.\n\ndef Ty.FitsL144–157 ↗#Recursive size bound B on a value: S.sz b x ≤ B on base sorts, bits n ≤ B on .nat, length and element bounds on .list, and pointwise bounds on .tbl.\n\nabbrev ValFitsL159–160 ↗#\n\ndef OpsSizeHonestL162–166 ↗#Size-honesty obligation on O: every operator o grows the Ty.Fits bound B by at most O.cost o.\n\n6 declarations not shown (lines 168–217): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesReductionDsl.Ty.BaseFits, ReductionDsl.OpsBaseBounded, ReductionDsl.Ty.listDepth, ReductionDsl.Ty.NoNestedLists, ReductionDsl.Ty.HasNoTbl, ReductionDsl.Ty.treeBlocks\n\ninductive ExprL219–264 ↗#Pure expressions in context Γ. Multiplication, division, and modulus allow only constant operands (mulK, divK, modK); bounded list combinators (*B) inspect at most the first K entries.\n\n\n\n7 declarations not shown (lines 269–278): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesReductionDsl.Expr.v0, ReductionDsl.Expr.v1, ReductionDsl.Expr.v2, ReductionDsl.Expr.v3, ReductionDsl.Expr.v4, ReductionDsl.Expr.v5, ReductionDsl.Expr.v6\n\ndef Expr.evalL280–323 ↗#Evaluates a pure expression in environment ρ.\n\ndef Expr.costL325–364 ↗#Static step cost of an expression: branches charge max of their arms, loops charge K times their body, and .tget/.tset charge 64/128.\n\ndef Expr.sizeL366–405 ↗#Syntax-tree size of an expression: counts both branch arms, each loop body once, bit-lengths of numeric literals and loop bounds, and O.opSize o for operator payloads.\n\ndef reductionSizeBudgetL407–409 ↗#Syntax-tree size budget (2 ^ 24 nodes) for headline-named reductions; bounds the non-uniform lookup-table advice an existentially quantified reduction can embed.\n\nstructure SamplersL411–418 ↗#Coin-only samplers (ProbComp, with no target queries) over typed domains and codomains with constant per-sampler step cost sCost.\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 420–435): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesReductionDsl.Samplers.empty, ReductionDsl.Samplers.sum\n\ndef SampSizeHonestL437–441 ↗#Size-honesty obligation on X: every sampled output grows the Ty.Fits bound B by at most X.sCost s.\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 443–493): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesReductionDsl.SampBaseBounded, ReductionDsl.Expr.costWithTbl\n\nstructure IfaceL495–508 ↗#Oracle interface into target specification T: typed query tags encoded as single T-queries with step cost qCost, uniform-coin forwarding fwdU of cost uCost, and samplers smp.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 510–512): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesReductionDsl.Iface.withSamp\n\ndef Iface.liftPL514–517 ↗#Lifts a coin-only ProbComp into OracleComp T by forwarding coin draws via I.fwdU.\n\n\n\ninductive CompL521–545 ↗#Monadic programs over O and I: pure returns, sequencing, branching, sampling, target queries, and statically bounded loops (n iterations or at most the first K list entries).\n\ndef iterML547–549 ↗#\n\ndef findMLL551–553 ↗#\n\ndef anyMLL555–557 ↗#\n\ndef mapMLL559–561 ↗#\n\ndef consumeFirstMLL563–569 ↗#Short-circuiting replacement of the first entry passing p by mark of it.\n\ndef foldMLL571–573 ↗#\n\ndef Comp.evalL575–598 ↗#Interprets a Comp program into OracleComp T.\n\ndef Comp.costL600–615 ↗#Static step cost of a program: branches charge max of their arms and loops charge n or K times their body.\n\ndef Comp.queriesL617–632 ↗#Static weighted upper bound on target queries (w) and samples (ws).\n\ndef Comp.sizeL634–649 ↗#Syntax-tree size of a program: counts both branch arms, each loop body once, and bit-lengths of loop bounds n and K.\n\nstructure GameCodecL651–658 ↗#Encoding of source-game G queries into Q (qenc) and decoding of R values into G answers (rdec), with per-query encoding/decoding overhead codecCost.\n\n\n\ndef handlerImplL662–669 ↗#Simulates unifSpec + G in state σ by forwarding coins via I.fwdU and answering G-queries with h (in context [σ, C.Q]).\n\nstructure CostedReductionL671–679 ↗#Single-stage black-box reduction against game G (codec C) with state σ: init maps reduction input rIn to (aIn, σ), handle maps (σ, C.Q) to (C.R, σ), and finish maps (σ, aOut) to out.\n\n\n\ndef CostedReduction.implL683–685 ↗#\n\ndef CostedReduction.evalL687–693 ↗#Runs reduction R once around adversary A on input x in OracleComp T.\n\ndef CostedReduction.totalCostL695–697 ↗#Upper bound on step cost outside A when A makes at most q total unifSpec + G queries.\n\ndef CostedReduction.totalQueriesL699–702 ↗#Weighted upper bound on target queries and samples when A makes at most q G-queries.\n\ndef CostedReduction.sizeL704–706 ↗#Total syntax-tree size of R (init, handle, and finish counted once each).\n\nTwo-stage reductions\n\ninductive MidL710–714 ↗#Stage-1 termination state: either A finished (done), or A paused (paused) at query t with stage-1 challenge output c, saved pause data p, state s, and continuation k.\n\nstructure TwoStageCostedReductionL716–735 ↗#Two-stage black-box reduction against G (codec C) for a target taking stage-1 output ch and supplying stage-2 input rIn2. In stage 1, handlePre either answers a G-query (inl) or pauses (inr) with (c, p, σ'), and chDone produces c if A finishes without pausing; in stage 2, resume answers the paused query from rIn2, handlePost answers subsequent queries, and finish computes the final output.In eval1 and eval2, fuel caps G-queries per stage (returning dflt on exhaustion) while coin draws are forwarded without consuming fuel; setting fuel := q when A makes at most q G-queries across both stages makes the fallback unreachable. See eval1Bounded and eval2Bounded for explicit coin and game-query fuel.\n\n\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.run1L739–755 ↗#Runs stage 1 on oa for at most fuel G-queries (coins forwarded via I.fwdU); returns .done dflt s on fuel exhaustion.\n\ndef runFuelL757–770 ↗#Runs oa under handler h for at most fuel G-queries (coins forwarded via I.fwdU); returns (dflt, s) on fuel exhaustion.\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.eval1L772–782 ↗#Executes stage 1 of R on adversary A and input x with G-query budget fuel and fallback output dflt; yields the target's stage-1 input and Mid state.\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.eval2L784–794 ↗#Resumes m with stage-2 target input y under G-query budget fuel and fallback dflt, then runs R.finish.\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.totalCostL796–800 ↗#Upper bound on step cost outside A across both stages when A makes at most q total unifSpec + G queries.\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.totalQueriesL802–807 ↗#Weighted upper bound on target queries and samples across both stages when A makes at most q G-queries.\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.sizeL809–812 ↗#Total syntax-tree size of R across all six stage components, counted once each.\n\nRun-local size premises\n\ndef AllGameQueriesFitL816–829 ↗#Run-local query-size bound: along every execution branch of oa, each game query .inr t satisfies C.Q.Fits B (C.qenc t) (coin queries .inl n are unconstrained). Adapted from an earlier definition by Swarat Chaudhuri.\n\ndef supportWhenL831–840 ↗#Outputs reachable by oa along execution branches where every oracle query t receives an answer u satisfying P t u (equals support oa when P is True).\n\ndef Iface.AnswerFitsL842–846 ↗#Run-local answer-size predicate: target answer u : T i decodes within Ty.Fits B under every tag g and input x with I.enc g x = i.\n\nInput-specialized per-query-kind cost bounds\n\ndef Expr.costAtL850–896 ↗#Input-specialized cost of evaluating e in ρ: matches Expr.cost, except ite, caseOpt, caseSum, and letE charge their guard or bound expression plus only the branch taken at ρ (bounded list loops still charge static body .cost).\n\ndef Comp.pureEval?L898–917 ↗#Evaluates an effect-free prefix of c in ρ; returns none if execution reaches a sample, target query, or monadic loop.\n\ndef Comp.costAtL919–944 ↗#Input-specialized cost of running c in ρ: branches charge only the arm taken at ρ, bind specializes its continuation when c.pureEval? ρ = some x (and charges static k.cost otherwise), and loops charge static body .cost.\n\ndef CostedReduction.ValidKindCostsL946–951 ↗#Per-kind handler cost bound: from any state s, handling game query t costs at most hCost (kind t) under costAt.\n\ndef CostedReduction.totalCostByKindL953–960 ↗#Step-cost bound outside A when A's G-queries are partitioned into n kinds with at most qKind i queries and handler cost hCost i for kind i (forwarded coin draws are not counted in qKind).\n\ndef CostedReduction.CostBoundedByKindL962–965 ↗#Existence of valid per-kind handler cost bounds hCost with R.totalCostByKind hCost qKind ≤ B.\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.ValidKindCostsL967–973 ↗#Two-stage per-kind handler cost bound covering both handlePre and handlePost.\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.totalCostByKindL975–982 ↗#Step-cost bound outside A across both stages when A makes at most qKind i G-queries of kind i in total (forwarded coin draws are not counted in qKind).\n\ndef TwoStageCostedReduction.CostBoundedByKindL984–988 ↗#Two-stage counterpart of CostedReduction.CostBoundedByKind.\n\n9 declarations not shown (lines 992–1097): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesReductionDsl.Comp.costWithTbl, ReductionDsl.GameCodec.FitsOn, ReductionDsl.GameCodec.BaseFitsOn, ReductionDsl.CostedReduction.totalCostBounded, ReductionDsl.TwoStageCostedReduction.run1Bounded, ReductionDsl.runFuelBounded, ReductionDsl.TwoStageCostedReduction.eval1Bounded, ReductionDsl.TwoStageCostedReduction.eval2Bounded, ReductionDsl.TwoStageCostedReduction.totalCostBounded\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Reductions/ReductionDsl/Core.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Reductions.ReductionDsl.Core/#file-Computational___Specifications___Reductions___ReductionDsl___Core"}});